From 0a69d345026633e8eb10a705bb291785d7fc5e1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:58:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(seo): stop soft-404 redirect, duplicate URLs and dead
 audit

Recovery work for the organic-ranking drop. No user-facing workflow
changes: / still opens the login form first.

- public/404.html: replace the meta-refresh + location.replace redirect
  with a real not-found page. Forwarding every unknown URL to / made
  Google treat them as soft 404s and repeated the sneaky-redirect
  pattern that the July cloaking code had already used.
- vite.config.ts: skip `public` when collecting rollup inputs. It is
  Vite's publicDir, so listing it as an input emitted a second copy of
  every SEO page under dist/public/ and published each one on two
  crawlable URLs.
- portal.html: mark the legacy root document noindex so it cannot
  compete with the real homepage for Showpay / Show pay / Showpay login.
- tests/seo-audit.mjs and user-app/css/login.css: both files had their
  entire contents committed twice. The audit crashed with a duplicate
  declaration SyntaxError, so the SEO guard had not run since it was
  added; the stale CSS copy overrode the login layout rules.
- Extend the audit with guards for all of the above plus primary
  keyword coverage.
- Cover "ShowPay customer support" and the spaced "Show pay" variant on
  the support page and the homepage FAQ.
